%% Source of truth for sse-reconnect.svg (the PostgreSQL-backed event path).
sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as Client (SDK, browser, curl)
    participant Server as Platform API /v1/platform/sessions/{id}/sse
    participant Events as Session events (PostgreSQL, by sequence)
    Client->>Server: GET …/sse
    Server-->>Client: connected
    Events-->>Server: event_A, event_B
    Server-->>Client: event_A, event_B (id on each durable event)
    Note over Client,Server: Stream closes: connection cycle, network drop, or timeout
    Note over Events: event_C and event_D are written while the client is away
    Client->>Server: GET …/sse?since_id=event_B
    Server-->>Client: connected
    Server->>Events: Read after event_B's sequence
    Events-->>Server: event_C, event_D
    Server-->>Client: Replay event_C, event_D
    Events-->>Server: New live events
    Server-->>Client: Continue live delivery
    Note over Client: Remember durable event IDs and deduplicate overlap
